findings.body:
In `organize_agent_history`, the `ToolPromptMessage` content now reads from `tool_inputs` instead of `tool_responses`. That means the model is shown the tool's arguments as if they were the tool's output, on every replayed turn that uses tools. `tool_responses` is parsed on the lines above and never read again.

::diff{file="api/core/agent/base_agent_runner.py" lines="500-504"}

This is a silent prompt-context corruption. It won't crash, and the existing integration tests only check that the rows persist, not what history gets built from them.

::callout{type="warning"}
The `ToolPromptMessage` content should be the observation for that tool, not its input.

::suggestion{file="api/core/agent/base_agent_runner.py" lines="502-502"}
content=str(tool_responses.get(tool, agent_thought.observation)),

`create_agent_thought` sets the message and answer price columns in opposite directions. `message_unit_price` becomes `Decimal(0)` and `message_price_unit` becomes `Decimal("0.001")`, but `answer_unit_price` becomes `Decimal("0.001")` and `answer_price_unit` becomes `Decimal(0)`. The original code set all four to `0`, and the `price_unit` columns are the ones that have the `0.001` server default.

::diff{file="api/core/agent/base_agent_runner.py" lines="319-326"}

If the unit price is the per-token rate, the answer side now carries a nonzero rate before any usage is recorded. Any cost computed from a row that is not overwritten later will be wrong. The two sides should follow the same pattern.

::callout{type="warning"}
I could not confirm from this diff whether the usage pipeline always overwrites `answer_unit_price`. Confirm that before deciding how urgent this is.

The new `AgentThoughtValidation` Pydantic model is defined but never instantiated or imported anywhere in the codebase, so it adds no validation. Its `Config` block also says it uses "Pydantic v1 syntax - should use ConfigDict(extra='forbid')" while setting `extra = "allow"`, which contradicts the comment. This reads as an unfinished experiment and will confuse the next reader.

::diff{file="api/core/agent/base_agent_runner.py" lines="52-65"}

Either wire it into `create_agent_thought` / `save_agent_thought` as real validation, or remove it along with the `pydantic` import.

The only test changes are removing `id=fake.uuid4()` from seven `MessageAgentThought(...)` constructors in the integration test. Those edits are required by `init=False`, but they don't exercise anything new. Nothing covers:

- the `organize_agent_history` tool-replay path, which is where the content regression above lives;
- `create_agent_thought` defaults and the `Decimal` / `CreatorUserRole` values it now writes;
- `save_agent_thought` when the existing `thought` is `None`, which is the case the None-safe accumulation was added for.

A test that asserted the replayed `ToolPromptMessage` content would have caught the first finding.
